# 2026-03-25 17:34:40.616605
+Rigorously analyze the entire Binder1.txt-file. This file is enormous and contains the latest version each Microsoft Exchange protocol. It is strictly forbidden to continue without having access to this file!!
+
+Then, rigorously analyze all other files which contain the full untruncated contents of every single file of the Exchange Gateway solution. 
+Provide me with the new/modified/replaced files to copy/paste into the Exchange Gateway solution, which you created, to close at least 10 of the gaps listed under: "Specific remaining gaps closed in this revision" in the file: GAP_ANALYSIS.md. Do not rename any files. 
+
+Note that "example.com" is not the actual domain I used, but is an example, instead of my actual domain.
+
+All new ".rs"-files will be placed by me in the existing "/src/" subfolder in the github repository. All new files must have a different name from existing filenames. Prefer adding your new code to existing files. 
+
+Rigorously ensure that your output is: 100% perfectly, completely, untruncated, no stubs, without any compromise and without any caveats perfectly, security hardened, production-ready, highly-robust, up-to-date per March 2026, fully and perfectly compatible. This github repository and its subfolders contains the latest version of full files of "exchange_gateway", used to create a docker container, for my entire complete specific use-case. 
+
+In the "Cargo.toml" file, the version of Rust (v1.94.0), edition (2024), and all dependencies are the latest version. These may not be lowered. 
+"Binder1.txt" which contains the latest version of the Exchange protocols from Microsoft must be used as the source of truth on these protocols. The Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container uses basic username/password authentication and connects over ipv4 and ipv6. This will not change.
+
+Specific use-case:
+The calendar of an existing Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container, with modifications to it's "config.toml"-file, and integrated with a number of free Cloudflare services, can be used full, natively, perfectly, without client side extensions in Outlook-client on Windows 11 as well as Android 15. This is achieved by a docker container written in Rust v1.94.0, running alongside the existing Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container, and a number of free Cloudflare services. 
+
+See outlook versions:
+(new) Outlook Windows 11 (v20251205004.10 is the latest stable version per February 2026. I verified)
+Outlook Android: (5.2607.0 is the latest stable version per February 2026. I verified)
+
+
+Note that the existing Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container uses RocksDB as it's backend, and therefore it's "config.toml"-file does not refer to the path of any tls-files. The existing Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container uses an ACME TLS certificate provider.
+
+I only use the website of Cloudflare to configure Cloudflare services. No connector, other than "cloudflared" installed on the Ubuntu server, will be created. The aforementioned "cloudflared" is currently used for a Cloudflare Tunnel to access the Stalwart Mailserver webui with a published application routes.
+
+Cloudflare tunnel configuration:
+
+-"https://exchange.mail.example.com/Microsoft-Server-ActiveSync": "http://[Ubuntu Server 24 LTS local ip]:8134"
+-"https://exchange.mail.example.com/EWS/*": "http://[Ubuntu Server 24 LTS local ip]:8134"
+-"https://stalwart.example.com": "http://[Ubuntu Server 24 LTS local ip]:8080" #used to access webui.
+
+Use Cloudflare (worker), at a minimum, for TLS terminal for the exchange_gateway docker container.
+
+Cloudflare worker: worker/index.js
+Name: exchange-gateway-db
+Route: "exchange.mail.example.com/api/*"
+Binding name: "EXCHANGE_DB". Value: "exchange_gateway_db"
+
+Cloudflare D1 SQL database: d1_schema.sql
+Name: exchange_gateway_db
+
+This is achieved by a docker container written in Rust v1.94.0, running alongside the existing Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container, and a number of free Cloudflare services. I only use the website of Cloudflare to configure Cloudflare services. 
+
+No connector, other than "cloudflared" installed on the Ubuntu server, will be created. The aforementioned "cloudflared" is currently used for a Cloudflare Tunnel to access the Stalwart Mailserver webui with a published application routes.
+
+Docker host: 
+Ubuntu Server 24 LTS up to date per March 2026. The docker host has the latest stable version of docker and cloudflared installed. 
+This "cloudlfared" is currently used to route: "https://stalwart.example.com" to the webui of the Stalwart Mailserver v0.15.5 container.
+
+Strictly use Binder1.txt as the source of truth on the latest Exchange protocol spec. Strictly adhere to my specific use-case. 
+
+Rigorously ensure that the gaps are closed: 100% perfectly, completely, untruncated, no stubs, without any compromise and without any caveats perfectly, security hardened, production-ready, highly-robust, up-to-date per March 2026, fully and perfectly compatible.

